quality falls from 95% to 85%; every hour the last window of judged answers is tested

  judged/hour   window  hours to notice  false alarms a week
            5      20h               18                  2%
           20       5h                6                  4%
           50       2h                3                  8%
          200       1h                2                  8%

At 5 judged answers an hour the test needs a 20-hour window to hold enough of them,
so a fall takes about 18 hours to show; at 200 an hour it takes about 2.
The false-alarm column is the share of healthy weeks with any alarm at all. Judge
calls cost money, and the hours between a fall and a page cost wrong answers:
choose the rate from the second, not the first.
